       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg add little blood-pressure benefit and raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia.\n\nPlease confirm which of these you want:\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose. This is also the usual dose if the patient is frail or you want to titrate up.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if it's intentional. If so, tell me the rationale to put in the order note, for example a specialist recommendation or a deliberate off-label plan.\n\nWas 20 mg a typo, or did you mean a different dose or a different drug? Once you confirm, I'll enter the order."
